## 12. Monetization and Enterprise Readiness

Design the front-end to make value legible and gates natural; final pricing numbers are Rohit's call (§16).

- **Tier scaffold:** Free (1 project, capped agent credits, Supaprod badge on shipped output) → Pro (individual: more credits, custom domains, full launch kit) → Team (seats, shared workspace memory, roles) → Enterprise (SSO/SAML, audit log, RBAC, private model routing, SLA). Wire the UI gating and upgrade surfaces; keep price points as config.
- **Usage-based agent credits** align cost with the metered model spend underneath — the natural unit for an agentic product. Show a calm usage meter in Settings; warn before caps, never interrupt mid-task.
- **Upgrade moments are earned, not popped:** at value peaks (project shipped, launch kit ready), one quiet line — "Take this live on your own domain → Pro." Never modal-block work.
- **Stickiness = accumulated memory + shipped history.** Make the workspace's learned conventions and shipped-product timeline *visible* in Settings/Workspace — the user should be able to see what they'd lose by leaving.
- **Trust surface:** audit log of every agent action and human approval, role-based permissions, data-handling summary. Reuse backend capabilities where they exist; flag gaps where they don't.

